        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.11,
            0.884,
            0.149
          ],
          "content": "The amount of paani in the cylindrical vessel is given by V = area of base × height."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.33,
            0.151,
            0.667,
            0.171
          ],
          "content": "V = \\pi   (10)(10) \\times 50 = 5000\\pi    cm ^3.",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.18,
            0.882,
            0.22
          ],
          "content": "To estimate the number of golgappas, two students went about in different ways:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.231,
            0.371,
            0.249
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Student 1’s calculation"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.263,
            0.491,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": "Estimated radius of an average golgappa is 1.5 cm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.317,
            0.473,
            0.374
          ],
          "content": "Volume of a golgappa = 3 ≈ 14.14 cm<sup>3</sup>."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.375,
            0.491,
            0.415
          ],
          "content": "(neglecting the thickness of the golgappa)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.426,
            0.494,
            0.502
          ],
          "content": "Assuming each golgappa is filled with 60% pani on an average, the volume of pani in a golgappa $1 4 . 1 4 \\times 0 . 6 \\approx 8 . 5 ~ \\mathrm { c m } ^ { 3 } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.515,
            0.492,
            0.579
          ],
          "content": "The number of golgappas that can be served $\\mathrm{is}=\\frac{5000\\pi}{8.5} \\approx 1848.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.582,
            0.492,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": "Lallan can serve about 1850 golgappas with the pani he has."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.507,
            0.23,
            0.748,
            0.249
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Student 2’s calculation"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.505,
            0.263,
            0.871,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": "Estimated radius of an average golgappa is 1.75 cm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.507,
            0.316,
            0.854,
            0.374
          ],
          "content": "4 Volume of a golgappa = × π (1.75)3 3 ≈ 22.43 cm<sup>3</sup>."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.505,
            0.375,
            0.87,
            0.415
          ],
          "content": "(neglecting the thickness of the golgappa)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.503,
            0.426,
            0.871,
            0.503
          ],
          "content": "Assuming each golgappa is filled with 80% pani on an average, the volume of pani in a golgappa $22.43 \\times 0.8 \\approx 18   cm ^3.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.504,
            0.515,
            0.87,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": "The number of golgappas that can be $\\mathrm{served~is} = \\frac{5000\\pi}{18} \\approx 873.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.505,
            0.582,
            0.871,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": "Lallan can serve about 870 golgappas with the pani he has."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.635,
            0.881,
            0.675
          ],
          "content": "We see that the final answer depends upon the assumptions, estimations, and approximations done in the process."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.68,
            0.613,
            0.816
          ],
          "content": "**Example 6:** Anirban saw a few tennis balls lying around. He wondered, “How many tennis balls can fit in an empty classroom?”. The classroom is of dimensions 30 ft × 30 ft × 15 ft. Estimate how many tennis balls of radius 3 cm fit in this classroom. Before calculating, make a guess."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.818,
            0.612,
            0.876
          ],
          "content": "The volume of the tennis ball is $\\frac{4}{3} \\times \\pi \\times 3^{3} \\approx 113  cm ^{3}$"
        },
